WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
A title page, being set
in type, letter by letter.

2
00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.660
Tess of the d'Urbervilles.

3
00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:10.390
Then, after a pause, a
second line slots in:

4
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.960
"A Pure Woman".

5
00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:15.000
Hardy added it after
reading the final proofs.

6
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.770
And around it, the
reviews begin to flutter.

7
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.200
Three words.

8
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.160
So why did they shock?

9
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:24.480
In this mission, you'll meet
the Victorian double standard,

10
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:28.370
in the novel and in the
divorce law of 1857.

11
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.010
You'll see how the magazine version
was changed for its readers.

12
00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.390
And you'll read how Hardy
defended his subtitle.

13
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.100
Your mission: explain
why the subtitle shocked.
